+
+## 4. Code changes
+
+One file: `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`. A new, self-contained mode, `MODE_SX8REF`, selected by the
+argv token `sx8ref`. No existing test case, descriptor, tolerance, or code path was modified.
+
+### 4.1 Why a new mode rather than a tolerance change
+
+Default `test` mode compares a backend against the **CPU backend**. For S-X8 that reference is itself
+lossy: the CPU traits give S-X8 `vec_dot_type = Q8_1`, so the CPU arm quantizes the **activations**
+to q8_1 before the dot, while the Vulkan mat-vec dequantizes weights and multiplies in f32. Two
+consequences, and they are the two things that blocked B2:
+
+1. The CPU backend refuses S-X8 x f16 outright (src1 must be f32 or the vec_dot type), so the twelve
+   f16-activation descriptors print `not supported [CPU]` and cover nothing. A decline is not
+   coverage.
+2. The 5e-4 NMSE bound in `test` mode is sized to absorb the CPU reference's own q8_1 activation
+   error. At m=1,n=1 the NMSE normalizes over a **single** output element, so that reference error is
+   not averaged down and the case sits on the bound.
+
+`sx8ref` replaces the reference instead of relaxing the bound.
+
+### 4.2 The reference
+
+- Weights are decoded with `dequantize_row_sx8()` via `ggml_get_type_traits(GGML_TYPE_SX8)->to_float`
+  — ggml's own S-X8 decoder, which is what the shader header names as its reference.
+- The dot product is accumulated in **double** against exact activations.
+- Neither arm of the reference is the kernel under test.
+- Inputs are fixed: `sx8_ref_value(row, i)` is a pure integer hash of (row, index), no RNG, no
+  `std::random_device`, no thread slicing. `init_tensor_uniform` could not be used — it seeds from
+  `random_device` and splits the range over `hardware_concurrency()` threads, so its bytes differ per
+  machine and per run. A case that fails here fails identically on the checker's machine.
+- The reference's threading partitions by **row range only**, so thread count cannot change the
+  result.
+- For f16 cases the f32 reference copy is rounded through f16 first, so the reference sees exactly
+  the activations the device sees. f16 to f32 is exact.
+
+### 4.3 Bounds — not loosened, and reported per path
+
+`sx8_ref_bound()`:
+
+| Path | Bound | Basis |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| dequant (`GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` unset/0) | NMSE <= **1e-9** | The kernel multiplies decoded weights by exact activations in f32 over k <= 5120 terms; expected NMSE is f32 round-off, order 1e-13..1e-12. 1e-9 sits three orders above that, and still four orders **below** the error a wrong decode gives (one mis-decoded 6-bit level moves a term by ~1 part in 64 of its range). |
+| q8_1 integer dot (`GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=1`) | NMSE <= **5e-4** | That path quantizes activations itself. Scored under its own number so the two paths are never averaged onto one bound. |
+
+The `test` mode 5e-4 bound is untouched. 1e-9 is **tighter** than the sweep bound, not looser.
+
+### 4.4 Near-zero diagnosis, separated from arithmetic error
+
+`sx8_ref_compute` also returns `ref_abs[i]`, the sum of the **term magnitudes** of that same dot
+product. An element is classified near-zero when `|ref[i]| < 1e-3 * ref_abs[i]` — that is, the dot
+product lost three or more digits to cancellation. Near-zero elements are excluded from `relmax` and
+reported separately as `nz=<count>/<total> nz_absmax=<value>`.
+
+The split is **per element against its own term sum**, not against the output RMS. A
+`1e-3 * rms(ref)` cut is structurally inert exactly where the diagnosis is needed: at m=1,n=1 there is
+one output element, so the test reduces to `|ref| < 1e-3*|ref|`, which is never true. This was
+corrected before the build.
+
+Every case reports, side by side: `nmse` (the same metric the sweep uses), `absmax` (absolute error),
+`relmax` (relative, near-zero excluded), `rms`, the near-zero count and its worst absolute error, and
+a CPU calibration column.
+
+### 4.5 The CPU calibration column
+
+Where the CPU backend accepts the case, `sx8ref` also runs it on CPU against the **same** independent
+reference and prints `cpu_nmse=... cpu_absmax=...`. This is **not** a pass/fail gate. It is the number
+that shows how much of the sweep's 5e-4 budget the CPU reference itself was spending. Where CPU
+declines (all f16 cases), the column prints the decline reason.
+
+### 4.6 Case list — 34 cases in three groups
+
+| Group | Cases | Shape |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `m1` | 10 | type_b=f32, m=1, n in {1,2,3,4,8}, k in {1056, 5120} — the ten reproducers, restored with fixed inputs |
+| `f32-twin` | 12 | type_b=f32, m in {7, 4095, 17408}, n in {1,2,3,8}, k=5120 |
+| `f16` | 12 | type_b=f16, same shapes and same data as the twins |
+
+Groups are ordered cheapest-first (`m1`, then m=7, m=4095, m=17408) and each f16 case is emitted
+immediately after its f32 twin, so a truncated run still leaves a usable, paired result set.
+`GGML_ARIFI_SX8REF_GROUPS` (substring match on the group name) selects a subset.
+
+The f32 twin is the **control**: same shape, same data, a path the CPU backend can run. If the f16
+group misses the bound while its twins pass, that discriminates f16 activation/accumulate precision in
+the shader from a bad reference. Whichever way that lands, the bound is not to be moved to
+accommodate it.
+
+A one-slot memo on `(m, k)` reuses the fill and the S-X8 quantize across the eight cases that share a
+weight matrix; without it the m=17408 group would re-fill and re-quantize 89M values eight times.
+
+### 4.7 A decline is counted as a failure
+
+In `sx8ref`, a backend declining a case prints `DECLINED` and increments **both** `n_declined` and
+`n_fail`. The purpose of the mode is that every listed descriptor executes against a reference, so a
+decline is a coverage failure, not a neutral skip.
+
+### 4.8 Planted-red reachability
+
+`GGML_ARIFI_SX8REF_PLANT_RED=1` flips one weight byte on the **device copy only**, after the reference
+has been computed and before `ggml_backend_tensor_set`. The device therefore sees different weights
+than the reference did, and **every case must go red**. A green planted run means the mode cannot
+detect a wrong kernel and its clean results mean nothing.
+
+**The planted run exits nonzero by design.** Any `.done` / exit-code wrapper must treat a nonzero exit
+from that specific invocation as the expected result, not as a harness failure.
