+# R46b B2 — S-X8 correctness, R3: planted-red reachability closure
+
+Working tree: `C:\ArifiLabs\cache\r46b-wt`, branch `lane-230/r46b-rebased-2026-09-11`,
+HEAD `06acb7f4f377a21e4cb2f6b3d712de23170cad30` (unchanged — nothing was committed, merged or
+promoted in R3). The only source change is uncommitted in `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`.
+
+## Verdict
+
+**B2 READY FOR SOL LOW CHECK**
+
+The R2 blocker is closed. The planted-red probe now goes red on **10/10** m=1 cases on **both**
+paths (`GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=0` and `=1`), including every k=5120 case. The worst case on the q8_1 path clears its
+5e-4 bound by 157x; the worst case on the dequant path clears its 1e-9 bound by 7.4e7x. Clean m=1 output is byte-identical to the pre-existing green receipts on
+both paths, so the injection is provably gated off. No bound, reference, production kernel,
+descriptor list or clean input was changed.
+
+---
+
+## 1. The R2 blocker, restated exactly
+
+Receipt `15-sx8ref-planted-red-mmvq` reported `10 cases executed, 0 declined, 5 failed`. The five
+k=1056 cases went red; the five k=5120 cases stayed inside the 5e-4 q8_1 bound at nmse
+1.973e-05 .. 1.878e-04. A probe that cannot go red on half its descriptors does not license the
+green result on those descriptors.
+
+**Root cause.** The injection was `a_dev[a_dev.size()/2] ^= 0xFF` — one byte in the whole weight
+buffer. The injected error energy is therefore a fixed absolute quantity divided by the output
+energy of the dot product, i.e. it scales as `1/(m*k)`. At k=1056 that cleared 5e-4; at k=5120,
+4.85x more terms diluted it below the bound. The old dequant-path receipt `12` went 10/10 red only
+because its bound is 1e-9, seven orders lower — same weak injection, more forgiving gate. The
+defect was in the probe's *shape dependence*, not in its direction.
+
+## 2. The fix
+
+`tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`, new helper `sx8_ref_plant_red()` (inserted immediately before
+`run_sx8_reference_slice`), replacing the one-line in-place XOR at the call site.
+
+```
+for each 30-byte S-X8 block b in the DEVICE COPY:
+    qh[b % 16] ^= 0x88
+```
+
+Three properties, each deliberate:
+
+| Property | How it is obtained | Why it matters |
+|---|---|---|
+| Shape-independent strength | one corrupted byte **per block**, not per buffer | corrupted fraction is a fixed 2 weights in 32 for every m and every k — the k=5120 dilution that caused the R2 block cannot recur |
+| Deterministic worst case | `^0x88` flips bit 3 of each 4-bit high nibble, i.e. bit 5 of each 6-bit level | **every** corrupted weight moves exactly 32 of 64 levels; no dependence on the stored value |
+| Device-copy-only | mutates the caller's `a_dev` copy, never the memoized `a_q` | the reference is computed before the call, from uncorrupted bytes; clean runs never enter the helper |
+
+`^0x88` was chosen over `^0xFF` on purpose. `^0xFF` maps a nibble to `15 - nibble`, so a stored
+nibble of 7 or 8 moves only 4 of 64 levels — a weak worst case papered over by an
+expected-value argument. That style of reasoning is what produced the R2 defect. `^0x88` makes the
+displacement a constant.
+
+### 2.1 Why the injected magnitude exceeds BOTH path bounds
+
+Documented in a source comment above the helper (not in this report alone), so the argument travels
+with the code:
+
+- `dequantize_row_sx8()` decodes `value = rlo + step * level`, `step = (r1 - r0)/63`, where the
+  2-bit `config` strategy selects a sub-range of width `R`, `R/4`, `R/4` or `R/2` of the block range
+  `R = dmax - dmin` (s=0..3, `ggml/src/ggml-quants.c:2394`). A level delta of 32 therefore displaces
+  the weight by `32/63 * width`. **Taken over the worst of the four strategies** that is
+  `32/63 * R/4 ~= 0.13*R` — no strategy is degenerate.
+- Inputs are uniform in [-1,1), so `R ~ 1.5` typical and the mean squared term is ~1/3. At a 1/16
+  corrupted fraction the NMSE floors near 7e-3: above 5e-4, and seven orders above 1e-9.
+- The bound function `sx8_ref_bound()` is untouched. Nothing here weakens a gate; it only guarantees
+  the probe crosses one.
+
+A layout guard sits at the top of the helper:
+`GGML_ASSERT(ggml_type_size(GGML_TYPE_SX8) == 30 && ggml_blck_size(GGML_TYPE_SX8) == 32)`, plus
+`a_dev.size() % bs == 0`. The `qh` offset of 5 is pinned to the `.sx8v43` container
+(`dmin`,`dmax` 2x2 B; `config` 1 B; `qh` 16 B; `ql` 8 B; `coeff` 1 B — `ggml/src/ggml-common.h:332`).
+The assert catches a size change; it does not catch a field reorder at constant size, and is not
+built out further because the container is pinned byte-identical upstream.
+
+### 2.2 Second change: the receipt now classifies itself
+
+Under plant, rc=1 is the *expected* outcome, so rc alone could not distinguish "all red" from
+"partly red" — receipt 15's block was found by a human counting FAIL lines. The slice now prints,
+in plant mode only:
+
+```
+  PLANTED RED reachability: <n_fail>/<n_run + n_declined> cases went red
+```
+
+and, when they are not equal, a distinct loud line `PLANTED RED NOT REACHED: N case(s) stayed
+inside the bound under corruption`. It prints rather than asserts, so a partial-red run still
+leaves a complete receipt instead of an aborted one.
+
