+## 1. Finding 1 — the bound now follows the route that executed, not the flag that was requested
+
+The defect: `run_sx8_reference_slice()` read `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ` once and labelled the whole run
+q8_1. The Vulkan backend quantizes activations only when `src1->type == GGML_TYPE_F32`
+(`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:11087`), so the twelve f16-activation descriptors always took
+the dequant route and were nonetheless scored at 5e-4 — a 500,000x relaxation on a path that is not
+q8_1 at all.
+
+The repair is a per-case route decision that mirrors the backend predicate:
+
+```
+sx8_ref_route_of(c, mmvq_requested):
+    q8_1  iff  mmvq_requested
+           &&  c.type_b == GGML_TYPE_F32          // 11087: src1 must be f32
+           &&  (c.n * c.k) % 4 == 0               // 11087: (ne11*ne10) % 4
+           &&  c.n <= 8                           // 11851: mul_mat_vec_max_cols, else the matmul path
+    dequant otherwise
+```
+
+`mmvq_requested` mirrors the dispatcher character for character: `GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ` first, then
+`GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ` (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:8297-8302`), then `env[0] == '1'` — not `atoi(env) != 0`, which
+the previous code used and which disagrees with the backend on `"2"` and `"01"`
+(`ggml-vulkan.cpp:10914`).
+
+The bound is then a function of the route only: dequant 1e-9, q8_1 5e-4. **F16 activations are gated
+at 1e-9 even when MMVQ is requested**, and the per-case output line now carries the route and the
+bound it was scored under:
+
+```
+MUL_MAT(type_a=sx8,type_b=f16,m=7,n=1,k=5120,grp=f16,route=dequant,bound=1e-09): nmse=1.472e-13 ... OK
+MUL_MAT(type_a=sx8,type_b=f32,m=7,n=1,k=5120,grp=f32-twin,route=q8_1,bound=0.0005): nmse=4.837e-05 ... OK
+```
+
+## 2. Finding 2 — a deterministic witness proves the route, and q8_1 is exercised on its own inputs
+
+The predicate above is a *prediction* of backend behaviour. It is checked against the measurement.
+
+Activation quantization costs ~8 bits per element and cannot hide. Measured on this box, same binary,
+same descriptors, the two routes are **eight orders apart** (worst dequant 1.472e-13 against smallest
+q8_1 1.306e-05):
+
+| Route | measured NMSE range | receipts |
+|---|---|---|
+| dequant | 2.355e-15 .. 1.472e-13 | 43 (m1), 40 (the twelve f16 cells) |
+| q8_1 | 1.306e-05 .. 6.606e-05 | 41 (m1), 40 (the twelve f32-twin cells) |
+
+So a q8_1-labelled case must also *measure* like q8_1. The witness floor is **1e-8** — 6.8e4x above
+the worst dequant reading (1e-8 / 1.472e-13), 1306x below the smallest q8_1 reading
+(1.306e-05 / 1e-8). A case that claims q8_1 and lands below
+the floor did not execute q8_1 (an unsupported `integer_dot_product` device, or a future routing
+change, produces exactly that) and is printed as `ROUTE MISMATCH` and counted as a FAILURE, not
+passed under the relaxed bound. The floor is vacuous under `PLANT_RED` — corruption lifts every case
+far above it — so it is disabled there, and the ledger says so.
+
+Every run now ends with a route ledger, which is the line the receipt is read on:
+
+```
+ROUTES: 12 executed on q8_1 (bound 0.0005, witness floor 1e-08), 12 on dequant (bound 1e-09); 0 route mismatch
+```
+
+**q8_1 is exercised on inputs that actually enter q8_1** — F32 activations with MMVQ requested — in
+two independent receipts: the ten m=1 mat-vec descriptors (41) and the twelve f32-twin descriptors at
+m=7/4095/17408 (40). The f16 half of receipt 40 is the control: same shapes, same weights, dequant
+route, 1e-9 bound, all green.
+
+The R3 planted-red mutation (`sx8_ref_plant_red()`, one level byte per 30-byte block, `^0x88`) is
+unchanged, and both planted receipts report **10/10** red. Precisely: the slice *prints* the
+`n_fail/n_total` reachability count and a loud `PLANTED RED NOT REACHED` line when they differ; it
+does not assert, so a partial-red run leaves a complete receipt instead of an aborted one (R3's stated
+reason, accepted by the R3 check). rc is 1 under plant either way, which is why the count, not rc, is
+the line to read.
