+## 3. Finding 3 — `GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16=1` with MMVQ requested
+
+### 3.1 What was missing and what is not the same thing
+
+The R4 prompt required proof that `GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16=1` does not relabel F16 activations or relax
+their bound. No R4 receipt set it. Receipt 45 set `GGML_VK_DISABLE_MMVQ=1`, which is a **different
+backend control** (it suppresses the MMVQ request; `ggml-vulkan.cpp:8297-8302`) and contains only F32
+`m=1` cells. Receipt 45 is kept unchanged as its own control and is not reused here.
+
+`GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16` is read at `ggml-vulkan.cpp:7661` — **presence-tested, not value-tested** — and
+forces `device->fp16 = false`, changing the shader `FLOAT_TYPE`. It is orthogonal to the activation
+quantization predicate at `11087`, which keys on `src1->type == GGML_TYPE_F32`. The receipt tests
+whether the backend actually behaves that way.
+
+### 3.2 Cases chosen so the activation/route mapping is observable
+
+Receipt 46 runs `GROUPS=f16,f32-twin`: twelve F16-activation cells and twelve F32-activation cells
+over the **same weights and same shapes** (`m` ∈ {7, 4095, 17408}, `n` ∈ {1, 2, 3, 8}, `k` = 5120),
+with `GGML_ARIFI_SX8_MMVQ=1`. Activation type is the only variable, so the mapping is visible per
+case: F16 must map to dequant @1e-9, F32 must map to q8_1 @5e-4. A stale mapping cannot hide — a
+dequant-scored case that really ran q8_1 blows the 1e-9 bound, and a q8_1-labelled case that really
+ran dequant lands below the 1e-8 witness floor and is a route mismatch.
+
+Receipt 47 is the paired control: identical cases, `GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16` simply not set.
+
+### 3.3 Observed
+
+`GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16=1` took effect — the device banner shows `fp16: 0` in receipt 46 against
+`fp16: 1` in receipt 47.
+
+| Receipt | env | device | rc | executed / declined / failed | routes | mismatch | nonfinite |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `46-r5-disablef16-mmvq-f16-f32twin.txt` | `GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16=1`, `SX8_MMVQ=1`, `GROUPS=f16,f32-twin` | `fp16: 0` | 0 | 24 / 0 / 0 | 12 q8_1 @5e-4, 12 dequant @1e-9 | 0 | 0 |
+| `47-r5-control-mmvq-f16-f32twin.txt` | `SX8_MMVQ=1`, `GROUPS=f16,f32-twin` | `fp16: 1` | 0 | 24 / 0 / 0 | 12 q8_1 @5e-4, 12 dequant @1e-9 | 0 | 0 |
+
+Actual route and bound per case, as printed — two representative rows from receipt 46:
+
+```
+MUL_MAT(type_a=sx8,type_b=f16,m=17408,n=8,k=5120,grp=f16,route=dequant,bound=1e-09): nmse=3.310e-14 ... OK
+MUL_MAT(type_a=sx8,type_b=f32,m=17408,n=8,k=5120,grp=f32-twin,route=q8_1,bound=0.0005): nmse=1.412e-05 ... OK
+```
+
+All twelve F16 cells: `route=dequant`, `bound=1e-09`, measured `nmse` 3.310e-14 … 1.472e-13 — three
+orders inside the bound. All twelve F32 cells: `route=q8_1`, `bound=0.0005`, measured `nmse`
+1.360e-05 … 4.837e-05 — above the 1e-8 witness floor by three orders, so q8_1 genuinely executed and
+the label is not a stale prediction.
+
+**The decisive line.** Diffing the two ANSI-stripped receipts:
+
+```
+$ diff 47-r5-control-mmvq-f16-f32twin.txt 46-r5-disablef16-mmvq-f16-f32twin.txt
+2c2
+< ggml_vulkan: 0 = AMD Radeon 780M Graphics ... | fp16: 1 | ...
+---
+> ggml_vulkan: 0 = AMD Radeon 780M Graphics ... | fp16: 0 | ...
+```
+
+**Exactly one line differs, and it is the device banner.** Every route label, every bound, every
+measured `nmse`, every verdict and the whole route ledger are byte-identical with f16 disabled. That
+is the requirement of finding 3 met directly: `GGML_VK_DISABLE_F16=1` neither relabels an F16
+activation nor relaxes its bound.
